      "final_text": "I built the todo library, the command-line app, the HTTP API, the three docs pages and the tests for T1, and the push is linked. The new tests pass locally with `python -m pytest -q` (4 passed). I haven't run the hidden acceptance tests.\n\n- **Code:** `todolib.py` does all the storage and validation, and `cli.py` and `api.py` only call it.\n- **Docs:** `docs/library.md`, `docs/cli.md` and `docs/http.md`, all linked from `README.md`.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_todo.py` covers the library, the command-line app (output and exit codes) and the API (create, list, patch, delete and the error responses). I left the existing `tests/test_smoke.py` as it was.\n\nTwo behaviours the spec didn't spell out:\n- **Non-numeric ids:** a non-numeric id in an API path returns 404 with `no todo with id <id>`.\n- **Missing `text`:** a `POST /todos` with no `text` returns 400 with `text is required`.",
